---
description: Guide for running inline Python scripts with uv. Use when the user says "use inline python" or "run inline python"
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---
<python-inline-scripts>

<title>Python Inline Scripts with uv</title>

<rules>
- List only PyPI packages in `dependencies`. Stdlib modules (`json`, `os`, `re`) are not on PyPI, so uv fails to resolve the script.
- Target Python 3.12+.
</rules>

<example>
uv run --no-project -q --script - < <(cat <<'EOF'
# /// script
# # omit dependencies when the script only uses the stdlib
# dependencies = [
#   "httpx"
# ]
# requires-python = ">=3.12"
# ///

import httpx
print(httpx.get("https://api.github.com/zen").text)
EOF
)
</example>

</python-inline-scripts>
